# Title: Potential Mpclient.DLL Sideloading Via Defender Binaries
# ID: 7002aa10-b8d4-47ae-b5ba-51ab07e228b9
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Bhabesh Raj
# Date: 2022-08-01
# Tags: attack.privilege-escalation, attack.persistence, attack.execution, attack.stealth, attack.t1574.001
# Description: Detects potential sideloading of "mpclient.dll" by Windows Defender processes ("MpCmdRun" and "NisSrv") from their non-default directory.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((process.executable:*\\MpCmdRun.exe OR process.executable:*\\NisSrv.exe)) AND NOT (((process.executable:C:\\Program Files (x86)\\Windows Defender\\* OR process.executable:C:\\Program Files\\Microsoft Security Client\\* OR process.executable:C:\\Program Files\\Windows Defender\\* OR process.executable:C:\\ProgramData\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Platform\\* OR process.executable:C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\*))))
